":{"publication_info":{"journal_volume":"34","artid":"690","page_start":"690","journal_title":"Nuovo Cim."}}},{"reference":{"publication_info":{"journal_volume":"80","artid":"797","page_start":"797","journal_title":"Phys.Rev."}},"curated_relation":false,"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/8579"}},{"reference":{"publication_info":{"journal_volume":"43","artid":"3147","page_start":"3147","journal_title":"Phys.Rev.D"}},"curated_relation":false,"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/320944"}},{"reference":{"publication_info":{"journal_volume":"4","artid":"2185","page_start":"2185","journal_title":"Phys.Rev.D"}},"curated_relation":false,"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/72671"}},{"reference":{"publication_info":{"journal_volume":"51","artid":"744","page_start":"744","journal_title":"Nuovo Cim.A"}}},{"reference":{"publication_info":{"journal_volume":"10","artid":"731","page_start":"731","journal_title":"Sov.Astron.Lett."}}},{"reference":{"publication_info":{"journal_volume":"7","artid":"985","page_start":"985","journal_title":"Class.Quant.Grav."}}}],"number_of_pages":18,"legacy_creation_date":"2010-01-04","preprint_date":"2010-01","author_count":2,"earliest_date":"2010-01","refereed":true,"external_system_identifiers":[{"schema":"MSNET","value":"2673791"},{"schema":"ADS","value":"2010CQGra..27r5007D"},{"schema":"SPIRES","value":"SPIRES-8511870"}],"facet_author_name":["1008217_Reinaldo J. Gleiser","1011485_Gustavo Daniel Dotti"],"_oai":{"sets":["Literature"],"id":"oai:inspirehep.net:841642","updated":"2025-06-27T13:46:21.646115"},"journal_title_variants":["Class. Quant. Grav.","Class.Quant.Grav."],"arxiv_eprints":[{"categories":["gr-qc"],"value":"1001.0152"}],"referenced_authors_bais":["V.Moncrief.1","A.Ishibashi.1","G.W.Gibbons.1","K.M.Simpson.1","T.Regge.1","Jacob.D.Bekenstein.1","R.G.Mclenaghan.2","W.Israel.1","Subrahmanyan.Chandrasekhar.1","J.Carminati.1","F.J.Zerilli.1","O.J.C.Dias.1","V.Cardoso.1","S.A.Hartnoll.1","M.Cavaglia.1","R.J.Gleiser.1","K.M.Case.1","M.Dafermos.1","M.Cadoni.1","I.F.Ranea.Sandoval.1","E.Poisson.1","J.A.Pullin.1","G.D.Dotti.1","Shijun.Yoshida.1","A.Anderson.2","H.Vucetich.1","P.Pani.1","Hideo.Kodama.1","Osamu.Seto.1","R.M.Wald.1","R.Penrose.1","R.H.Price.1","J.A.Wheeler.1"],"figures":[{"filename":"rnpd2.png","caption":"Penrose diagram for the maximal analytic extension of the \\rn space-time. All regions labeled I are isometric, and so are those labeled II, and III. Regions I and III are stationary, and region I is known to be linearly stable. The function $r$ is globally defined, with $r_o<r$ in I , $r_i<r<r_o$ in II , and $0<r<r_i$ in III. Also $r \\to \\infty$ at the conformal boundaries ${\\cal J}^{\\pm}$. The $r=\\ri$ horizon drawn thicker is a Cauchy horizon for the initial data surface $S$, the ${\\mathbb C}^{\\infty}$ extension beyond it (in particular, the two copies of region III just above it being non unique, unless analyticityof the metric is required.","source":"arxiv","key":"c8745aa84d4ccbc86c526603bd804bcf","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/c8745aa84d4ccbc86c526603bd804bcf"},{"filename":"V1S.png","caption":"Scalar potentials $V_1^+$ (left) and $V_2^+$ (right) for $\\ell=2, \\ri=1, \\ro=2$ plotted against $x$. The $x$ range was chosen in each case to exhibit the relevant details, beyond these ranges the behavior isthat captured in equations (\\ref{asymp})","source":"arxiv","key":"6fb8ad8b0f4e4623f54f2ac8351a42da","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/6fb8ad8b0f4e4623f54f2ac8351a42da"},{"filename":"V2S.png","caption":"Scalar potentials $V_1^+$ (left) and $V_2^+$ (right) for $\\ell=2, \\ri=1, \\ro=2$ plotted against $x$. The $x$ range was chosen in each case to exhibit the relevant details, beyond these ranges the behavior isthat captured in equations (\\ref{asymp})","source":"arxiv","key":"5a2f3e6d1978b6e3fe445a1d5f9bad27","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/5a2f3e6d1978b6e3fe445a1d5f9bad27"},{"filename":"V1V.png","caption":"Vector potentials $V_1^-$ (left) and $V_2^-$ (right) for $\\ell=2, \\ri=1, \\ro=2$ plotted against $x$.","source":"arxiv","key":"9aef3cff848c52e57be2483a1e393bde","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/9aef3cff848c52e57be2483a1e393bde"},{"filename":"V2V.png","caption":"Vector potentials $V_1^-$ (left) and $V_2^-$ (right) for $\\ell=2, \\ri=1, \\ro=2$ plotted against $x$.","source":"arxiv","key":"a4bbc1d8715516c09ee0d1bbc9587ecd","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/a4bbc1d8715516c09ee0d1bbc9587ecd"},{"filename":"hvplot.png","caption":"$\\ell=2$ potential $\\hat V$ -continuous line- for the transformed Zerilli equation (\\ref{hz}), and the transformed of the unstable mode $\\chi_1^+$. In this example $r_i=1$ and$r_o=2$.","source":"arxiv","key":"5f62d74ddca8a421f4ac98ba7221a7ed","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/5f62d74ddca8a421f4ac98ba7221a7ed"}],"legacy_version":"20180615180626.0","inspire_categories":[{"term":"Gravitation and Cosmology"}],"first_author":{"full_name":"Dotti, Gustavo","last_name":"Dotti","first_name":"Gustavo","recid":1011485},"control_number":841642,"dois":[{"value":"10.1088/0264-9381/27/18/185007"}],"document_type":["article"],"texkeys":["Dotti:2010uc"],"abstracts":[{"source":"arXiv","value":"Reissner--Nordstr\\'om black holes have two static regions: $r > \\ro$ and $0 < r < \\ri$, where $\\ri$ and $\\ro$ are the inner and outer horizon radii. The stability of the exterior static region has been established long time ago. In this work we prove that the interior static region is unstable under linear gravitational perturbations, by showing that field perturbations compactly supported within this region will generically excite a mode that grows exponentially in time. This result gives an alternative reason to mass inflation to consider the space time extension beyond the Cauchy horizon as physically irrelevant, and thus provides support to the strong cosmic censorship conjecture, which is also backed by recent evidence of a linear gravitational instability in the interior region of Kerr black holes found by the authors. The use of intertwiners to solve for the evolution of initial data plays a key role, and adapts without change to the case of super-extremal \\rn black holes, allowing to complete the proof of the linear instability of this naked singularity. A particular intertwiner is found such that the intertwined Zerilli field has a geometrical meaning -it is the first order variation of a particular Riemann tensor invariant-. Using this, calculations can be carried out explicitely for every harmonic number.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"arXiv"}}],"primary_arxiv_category":["gr-qc"],"titles":[{"title":"Gravitational instability of the inner static region of a Reissner-Nordstrom black hole"},{"source":"arXiv","title":"Gravitational instability of the inner static region of a Reissner-Nordstrom black hole"}],"curated":true},"id":"841642"},{"updated":"2023-03-07T03:41:15.456408+00:00","created":"2011-10-10T00:00:00+00:00","links":{"bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/931177?format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/931177?format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/931177?format=latex-us","json":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/931177?format=json","json-expanded":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/931177?format=json-expanded","cv":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/931177?format=cv","citations":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A931177"},"metadata":{"citation_count":119,"authors":[{"full_name_unicode_normalized":"aretakis, stefanos","full_name":"Aretakis, Stefanos","record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/authors/1069808"},"affiliations":[{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/institutions/902712"},"value":"Cambridge U."}],"last_name":"Aretakis","ids":[{"schema":"INSPIRE BAI","value":"S.Aretakis.1"}],"signature_block":"ARATACs","uuid":"30972c8e-3187-40fc-a174-379c0e70764e","first_name":"Stefanos","recid":106