mogeneous media"],"authors":[{"full_name":"Yang, S."}]}},{"reference":{"arxiv_eprint":"1312.7265","label":"63","publication_info":{"year":2013},"misc":["Global solutions of nonlinear wave equations with large energy"],"authors":[{"full_name":"Yang, S."}]}},{"reference":{"arxiv_eprint":"1312.7264","label":"64","publication_info":{"year":2013},"misc":["On the quasilinear wave equations in time dependent inhomogeneous media"],"authors":[{"full_name":"Yang, S."}]}}],"number_of_pages":74,"referenced_authors_bais":["M.Dafermos.1","N.Tanahashi.1","K.Murata.1","H.S.Reall.1","J.Lucietti.1","A.Ishibashi.1","J.Kommemi.2","Helmut.Friedrich.1","Y.Shlapentokh.Rothman.1","S.Hollands.1","J.Sbierski.1","S.Dain.1","S.Aretakis.1","G.D.Dotti.1","I.Rodnianski.1","P.Bizon.1"],"figures":[{"filename":"penrose-rn.png","caption":"The shaded region is the domain of outer communications, while its complement is the black hole region.","source":"arxiv","key":"e832a8e30073fa955c3c619cbe917304","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/e832a8e30073fa955c3c619cbe917304"},{"filename":"spacelike.png","caption":"spacelike","source":"arxiv","key":"203ee733b458a7ec23c0f846505c2188","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/203ee733b458a7ec23c0f846505c2188"},{"filename":"spacelike-null.png","caption":"spacelike-null","source":"arxiv","key":"be89c69b4bf8bec127e176f9839337b1","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/be89c69b4bf8bec127e176f9839337b1"},{"filename":"spacelike-coord.png","caption":"spacelike-coord","source":"arxiv","key":"e3256d39d5e1ec80081b40119bc9164d","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/e3256d39d5e1ec80081b40119bc9164d"},{"filename":"auarea.png","caption":"The arrows show the domains of integration in $u$ and $v$ that were used in the previous computations.","source":"arxiv","key":"5d627da6e8a7661574302da28764b650","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/5d627da6e8a7661574302da28764b650"},{"filename":"auarea1.png","caption":"The arrows show the domains of integration (in $v$) used for the boundedness of $\\dfrac{\\zeta}{\\nu}$, where $u'$ is always taken to be $0 \\mik u' \\mik U$. The constant $v''$ is taken to be $0 &lt; v'' \\mik v'$. Note that since $v' \\mik V$ and $V$ can be infinite, the $L^2$ integrability of $\\psi$ in the bootstrap region (where Theorem \\ref{dwee} applies) is crucial for our computations.","source":"arxiv","key":"8b601679303ac50ebb4e847a166c319f","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/8b601679303ac50ebb4e847a166c319f"},{"filename":"fsp.png","caption":"By the finite speed of propagation we have that $supp (\\psi ) \\subset \\Delta$. The area $\\Delta$ is covered also by the the spacelike-null foliation $\\{ \\Sigma_{\\tau} \\}_{\\tau \\meg 0}$, while the two different foliations coincide up to $r \\mik R_0$.","source":"arxiv","key":"92d20fbba9c11ae947b472c3b7701934","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/92d20fbba9c11ae947b472c3b7701934"},{"filename":"penrose-null.png","caption":"penrose-null","source":"arxiv","key":"e1aa8daf2682bec6b01d5d744b41f017","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/e1aa8daf2682bec6b01d5d744b41f017"}],"legacy_version":"20210316095709.0","inspire_categories":[{"term":"Gravitation and Cosmology"},{"term":"Math and Math Physics"}],"legacy_creation_date":"2014-08-21","preprint_date":"2014-08-19","author_count":1,"first_author":{"full_name":"Angelopoulos, Yannis","last_name":"Angelopoulos","first_name":"Yannis","recid":2284706},"control_number":1311597,"earliest_date":"2014-08-19","document_type":["article"],"texkeys":["Angelopoulos:2014bga"],"abstracts":[{"source":"arXiv","value":"We study spherically symmetric solutions of semilinear wave equations in the case where the nonlinearity satisfies the null condition on extremal Reissner--Nordstrom black hole spacetimes. We show that solutions which arise from sufficiently small compactly supported smooth data prescribed on a Cauchy hypersfurace \\widetilde{{\\Sigma}}_0 crossing the future event horizon \\mathcal{H}^{+} are globally well-posed in the domain of outer communications up to and including \\mathcal{H}^{+}. Our method allows us to close all bootstrap estimates under very weak decay results (compatible with those known for the linear case). Moreover we establish a certain number of non-decay and blow-up results along the horizon \\mathcal{H}^{+} which generalize known instability results for the linear case. Our results apply to spherically symmetric wave maps for a wide class of target spaces.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"arXiv"}}],"primary_arxiv_category":["math.AP"],"titles":[{"source":"arXiv","title":"Nonlinear Wave Equations With Null Condition On Extremal Reissner-Nordström Spacetimes I: Spherical Symmetry"}],"facet_author_name":["2284706_Yannis Angelopoulos"],"license":[{"imposing":"arXiv","url":"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/"}],"_oai":{"sets":["Literature"],"id":"oai:inspirehep.net:1311597","updated":"2023-03-06T17:00:28.695809"},"curated":false,"arxiv_eprints":[{"categories":["math.AP","gr-qc"],"value":"1408.4478"}]},"id":"1311597"}],"total":8},"links":{"self":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=...linear%20instability%20of%20the%20Reissner-Nordstrom%20Cauchy%20horizon...&size=10&page=1","bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=...linear%20instability%20of%20the%20Reissner-Nordstrom%20Cauchy%20horizon...&size=10&page=1&format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=...linear%20instability%20of%20the%20Reissner-Nordstrom%20Cauchy%20horizon...&size=10&page=1&format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=...linear%20instability%20of%20the%20Reissner-Nordstrom%20Cauchy%20horizon...&size=10&page=1&format=latex-us","json":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=...linear%20instability%20of%20the%20Reissner-Nordstrom%20Cauchy%20horizon...&size=10&page=1&format=json","json-expanded":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=...linear%20instability%20of%20the%20Reissner-Nordstrom%20Cauchy%20horizon...&size=10&page=1&format=json-expanded","cv":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=...linear%20instability%20of%20the%20Reissner-Nordstrom%20Cauchy%20horizon...&size=10&page=1&format=cv"}}